index 9de8922..6315091 100644
--- a/CAPTAIN.md
+++ b/CAPTAIN.md
@@ -20,3 +20,9 @@ Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History
 - Routing via `hashchange` event on `window`, filtering at model level
 - No external dependencies beyond todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css (devDependencies already installed: @cucumber/cucumber, happy-dom)
 - The test harness (`features/support/world.js`) loads `index.html` and `js/app.js`, executes via happy-dom `window.eval`, and fires DOMContentLoaded/load events
+
+## Voyage 2 — DOM identity and escape-cancel fixes
+
+**Root cause 1: DOM element identity destroyed on every render.** `render()` in `js/app.js` uses `dom.todoList.innerHTML = ''` and recreates all `<li>` elements from scratch on every state change (toggle, toggle-all, clear-completed). A real browser holds a reference to an element; after `render()`, that reference is detached from the DOM. Cypress reports `element-has-detached-from-dom`. Fix: preserve element identity by updating existing `<li>` elements in place (toggle class, update checkbox) instead of destroying and recreating the entire list.
+
+**Root cause 2: Escape key does not cancel edits in real browsers.** In a real browser, pressing Escape on the focused edit input fires `blur` before `keydown`. The `blur` handler calls `editTodo()` which commits the edit to the data model. Then the `keydown` handler sets `editingId = null` and re-renders, but the data is already changed. The in-harness suite masks this because it dispatches `keydown` before `blur`. Fix: track Escape key state and guard the blur handler so it skips the commit when Escape was just pressed.
