diff --git a/specs/dom-identity.feature b/specs/dom-identity.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..42f4c98
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/dom-identity.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Feature: DOM element identity preservation
+  As a user interacting with the todo list
+  I want the app to update existing elements in place when state changes
+  So that my browser's reference to an element remains valid across interactions
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves its DOM element identity
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo element is captured
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the captured element is still attached to the DOM
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Marking all as complete preserves DOM element identities
+    Given the app has todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo element is captured
+    And the "Clean house" todo element is captured
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then the captured element is still attached to the DOM
+    And all todos have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking all preserves DOM element identities
+    Given the app has completed todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo element is captured
+    And the "Clean house" todo element is captured
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then the captured element is still attached to the DOM
+    And no todos have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking a completed todo preserves its DOM element identity
+    Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo element is captured
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the captured element is still attached to the DOM
+    And the "Buy groceries" todo does not have class "completed"
