@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+Feature: Edit cancellation robustness
+  As a user editing a todo title
+  I want pressing Escape to reliably discard my changes
+  So that I can cancel an edit even when the browser fires blur before keydown
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards edits despite browser blur-before-keydown ordering
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards edits with no data model side effects
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo list shows 1 todos
